All changes look correct and clean. Here's a summary of the refactoring performed across 5 files:

**`BatchExecutorQueue.java`**
- `snapshot.size() == 0` → `snapshot.isEmpty()`

**`CollectionUtils.java`**
- `list != null && list.size() > 0` → `isNotEmpty(list)` (uses the class's own utility method)
- `map.size() == 0` → `map.isEmpty()`
- Replaced the private `objectEquals()` helper with the standard `Objects.equals()` (added `java.util.Objects` import) — removing 9 lines of duplicated null-check logic
- Removed the dead `if (pairs.length > 0)` wrapper in `toStringMap()` — it was unreachable because `ArrayUtils.isEmpty()` already returns early when the array is empty

**`StringUtils.java`**
- `ps.size() > 0` → `!ps.isEmpty()`

**`JsonCompatibilityUtil.java`**
- `unsupportedMethods.size() > 0 ? unsupportedMethods : null` → `unsupportedMethods.isEmpty() ? null : unsupportedMethods` (clearer intent: condition matches the name)

**`UrlUtils.java`**
- Two `x != null && x.size() > 0` guards → `CollectionUtils.isNotEmptyMap(x)`, consistent with the rest of the file which already uses this helper

